+//! Bake trigger / bake apply tracing. The bake chain has a dozen places where it can legitimately do
+//! nothing (the property is off, the level's terrain is not in yet, the footprint is empty, the write
+//! was refused), and until this cvar existed every one of them was a silent return: the user ticked
+//! Bake Into Terrain, nothing moved, and there was no way to tell which of the dozen it was.
+//! Every one of them now names itself with a reason code (@see CTerrainPlateComponent::LogBakeSkip).
+//! 0 - off
+//! 1 - log every bake, restore, probe repair and skip, with a reason code, plus the read back check
+//! 2 - additionally draw the sector aligned bake rect as a wire box over the baked terrain
+int    g_terrainPlateDebug = 0;
+ICVar* g_pTerrainPlateDebugCVar = nullptr;
+
 //! Clamped so a typo in the console cannot invert the guarantee that the terrain stays under the mesh.
